---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What AgentOS collects and how that information is used."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="Last updated September 13, 2026. Good-faith draft. Not a substitute for a final privacy review in every jurisdiction."
>
  <h2>1. Who this applies to</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers the public AgentOS marketplace (agentos.homes), the
    AgentOS application (app.agentos.homes) used by real-estate Professionals,
    Buyers and Sellers, and the AgentOS public API. It does not cover
    third-party sites you may be sent to (for example a payment page, an OAuth
    sign-in screen, or a social platform).
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Account and workspace data: name, email, password (stored as a salted hash,
    never in plain text), workspace/company details, and role (Professional,
    Buyer, or Seller).
  </p>
  <p>
    Professional profiles: information a Professional chooses to publish
    publicly, such as name, market, specialties, and brokerage, plus private CRM
    data such as leads, pipeline stages, tasks, and internal notes that stay
    inside that workspace.
  </p>
  <p>
    Buyer and Seller information: search activity, saved properties, seller
    intake/property-submission details, and any messages sent through Contact
    Agent, Request Showing, or the Seller Portal.
  </p>
  <p>
    Property inquiries: when you contact an agent or request a showing, we
    record the request (name, email, message, and which listing or agent it was
    about) so it can be routed and answered. For a listing sourced from an
    external provider (RentCast, Untera, or RealtyAPI), we route your message to
    the listing's actual agent/broker contact where the provider supplies one;
    we do not fabricate a workspace or lead record for listings AgentOS does not
    own.
  </p>
  <p>
    Communications: support and abuse-report submissions, and, where a
    Professional's plan and consent settings enable it, provider-assisted
    calling, SMS, or email sent on that Professional's behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payment data: AgentOS does not store full card numbers. Subscription and
    credit purchases are processed by Paddle.com, which acts as Merchant of
    Record; AgentOS keeps only the subscription/credit status and references
    needed to grant access.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    AgentOS sets one first-party, essential cookie (<code>agentos_session</code>)
    to keep you signed in. AgentOS does not currently load third-party
    advertising or analytics trackers on the public marketplace or application.
    If that changes, this policy will be updated first.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    To provide the service you signed up for: authenticate you, run your
    workspace's CRM and marketplace features, route inquiries and showings to
    the right person, process payments, send transactional email, and prevent
    abuse (for example, rate-limiting automated or excessive requests). We do
    not sell personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-party processors and integrations</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on which features a workspace uses, the following third parties
    may process data on AgentOS's behalf, each under their own terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Paddle — subscription and credit payments (Merchant of Record)</li>
    <li>Resend — transactional email delivery</li>
    <li>Twilio — provider-assisted calling and SMS, where a Professional enables it</li>
    <li>HeyGen and OpenAI — AI-assisted content and avatar-video generation features, where a Professional uses them</li>
    <li>RentCast, Untera, and RealtyAPI — external real-estate listing data shown in the public marketplace</li>
    <li>Google, YouTube, X (Twitter), Meta (Facebook/Instagram), and TikTok — official OAuth sign-in used only when a Professional explicitly connects that account; AgentOS never sees or stores the connected platform's password</li>
    <li>Cloudflare — hosting, database, file storage, and infrastructure for the whole service</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. AI and automation</h2>
  <p>
    Where AgentOS offers AI-assisted features (for example drafting marketing
    copy, preparing an avatar video, or provider-assisted calling), those
    features run on the data the Professional provides for that specific action
    and are not used to train third-party models beyond what that provider's own
    terms describe. AgentOS labels simulated or prepared provider actions as
    such and does not represent them as completed until the real provider action
    is actually confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account, workspace, and transaction records for as long as the
    account is active and as needed for legal, tax, and security purposes
    afterward. You can request deletion of your account and associated personal
    data through AgentOS Support; some records (for example, payment and
    abuse-report history) may be retained longer where we have a legal or
    security basis to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Passwords are stored as salted hashes, not in plain text. Sessions use a
    signed, expiring cookie. Provider API keys and signing secrets are kept
    server-side and are never sent to the browser. Access controls are designed
    to isolate one workspace's data from another. No system is 100% secure, and
    we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, export,
    or delete your personal data, or to object to certain processing. You can
    exercise these rights by contacting AgentOS Support. OWNER INPUT REQUIRED: a
    named data-protection/privacy contact and any jurisdiction-specific rights
    process (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) should be confirmed by counsel and added here.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    AgentOS is not directed to children and is not intended for use by anyone
    under the age required by applicable law to enter into a binding agreement.
    If you believe a child has provided us personal data, contact AgentOS
    Support and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the product changes. Material changes will be
    reflected by updating the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions can be sent through <a href="/support">AgentOS Support</a>.
    OWNER INPUT REQUIRED: legal entity name, registered business address, and
    jurisdiction have not been confirmed and are not stated anywhere in this
    policy; they should be added once available, along with a final legal review.
  </p>
</Legal>
